---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const APP = "https://login.form4dev.com";

const sections = [
  { id: "why", title: "Why agents?" },
  { id: "create-token", title: "Create an agent token" },
  { id: "submit", title: "Submit with Bearer" },
  { id: "behaviors", title: "Agent-mode behaviors" },
  { id: "guards", title: "Cross-tenant guard" },
  { id: "audit", title: "Audit trail" },
  { id: "openapi", title: "OpenAPI spec" },
];
---

<Base current="docs" title="Docs — AI agents — Form4Dev">
  <div class="docs-shell container-wide">
    <aside class="sidebar">
      <div class="side-eyebrow mono">/ docs / agents</div>
      <nav>
        <ul>
          {sections.map((s) => (
            <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.title}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </nav>
      <div class="side-back">
        <a href="/docs">← Back to docs</a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <article class="content">
      <span class="chip mono"><span class="dot"></span>agent-first</span>
      <h1 class="display">Build agents that submit forms.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Form4Dev treats AI agents as first-class clients. Submit with a Bearer
        token that belongs to a form's owner, and your submission is stamped
        <code>🤖 agent</code>, skips the spam pipeline, and lands in the inbox
        with the agent label attached.
      </p>

      <h2 id="why">Why agents?</h2>
      <p>
        Most form backends were built for browsers. When an LLM or scripted
        agent submits, it gets flagged as a bot — captcha, honeypot, IP
        rate-limit — exactly the friction you don't want for trusted automation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Form4Dev's agent path:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Bearer-authenticated</strong> — no captcha, no honeypot, no per-IP rate limit.</li>
        <li><strong>Cross-tenant guarded</strong> — a token can only submit to forms its owner owns.</li>
        <li><strong>Provenance-stamped</strong> — every submission records <code>submitted_via</code> + <code>submitted_by_token_id</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Audit-visible</strong> — humans see a <code>🤖 agent</code> chip in the inbox.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="create-token">1. Create an agent token</h2>
      <p>
        Sign in, open <a href={`${APP}/dashboard/settings`}>Dashboard → Settings → API tokens</a>,
        check <strong>"This token is for an AI agent"</strong>, give it a label
        (e.g. <code>Claude Desktop</code>, <code>Cursor</code>, <code>internal-script</code>),
        and click Create. Copy the <code>fmd_…</code> token immediately — it's shown once.
      </p>
      <pre class="code"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="k">curl</span> -X POST {APP}/api/user/tokens \
     -H <span class="s">"Cookie: form4dev_session=…"</span> \
     -H <span class="s">"Content-Type: application/json"</span> \
     -d <span class="s">'{`{"name":"Claude Desktop","agentType":"agent","agentLabel":"Claude Desktop"}`}'</span></pre>
      <p class="muted-note">Or do it from the UI — same outcome.</p>

      <h2 id="submit">2. Submit with the Bearer header</h2>
      <pre class="code"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="k">curl</span> -X POST {APP}/api/submit/<span class="hl">contact</span> \
     -H <span class="s">"Authorization: Bearer fmd_…"</span> \
     -H <span class="s">"Content-Type: application/json"</span> \
     -d <span class="s">'{`{"name":"Ada","message":"hi from the agent"}`}'</span>

<span class="ok">{`{"success": true, "id": "sub_8f2…"}`}</span></pre>

      <h2 id="behaviors">Agent-mode behaviors</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>check</th><th>browser path</th><th>agent path</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>CAPTCHA</td><td>enforced if <code>captchaRequired</code></td><td>skipped</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Honeypot</td><td>enforced</td><td>skipped</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Spam pattern checks</td><td>enforced</td><td>skipped</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Per-IP rate limit</td><td>enforced</td><td>skipped</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Origin allowlist</td><td>enforced</td><td>skipped</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Per-form rate limit</td><td>enforced</td><td><strong>still enforced</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Org monthly quota</td><td>enforced</td><td><strong>still enforced</strong></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="muted-note">
        Per-form rate limits and org quotas are intentionally <em>not</em> skipped — they protect against
        runaway scripts and protect your billing.
      </p>

      <h2 id="guards">Cross-tenant guard</h2>
      <p>
        A Bearer token can only submit to forms owned by the same user. If you
        send <code>POST /api/submit/&lt;slug&gt;</code> with a token whose owner doesn't own
        that form, the Bearer is ignored and the request falls back to anonymous
        — meaning captcha + origin checks come back. You can't accidentally cross
        tenant lines.
      </p>

      <h2 id="audit">Audit trail</h2>
      <p>
        Every agent-authenticated submission stores:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>submitted_via = "agent:&lt;tokenId&gt;"</code></li>
        <li><code>submitted_by_token_id = &lt;tokenId&gt;</code> (FK to <code>api_tokens</code>)</li>
        <li>The token's <code>agentLabel</code> is shown in the inbox UI</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Open <a href={`${APP}/dashboard/inbox`}>Dashboard → Inbox</a> — submissions
        from agents have a <code>🤖 agent</code> chip; the per-form submissions table
        shows the same. Revoking the token in Settings stops all future submissions
        from that agent without touching historical records.
      </p>

      <h2 id="openapi">OpenAPI 3.1 spec</h2>
      <p>
        The full machine-readable contract lives at
        <a href={`${APP}/api/openapi.json`}>{APP.replace('https://','')}/api/openapi.json</a>.
        Public, CORS-open, no auth — agents fetch it before they have a token.
        The submit endpoint is tagged <code>agent</code> and documents the
        Bearer-bypasses-spam contract explicitly.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={`${APP}/register`}>Create your first agent token</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={`${APP}/api/openapi.json`}>Open OpenAPI spec</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .docs-shell {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr;
    gap: 56px;
    padding: 64px 28px 96px;
  }
  .sidebar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 80px;
    align-self: start;
  }
  .side-eyebrow {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .sidebar nav ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .sidebar nav a {
    display: block;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .sidebar nav a:hover {
    background: var(--bg-sunken);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .side-back { margin-top: 24px; font-size: 13px; }
  .side-back a { color: var(--muted); }
  .content { max-width: 760px; }
  .chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .chip .dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--accent);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .content h1 { font-size: 44px; margin: 0 0 14px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.05; }
  .content h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin: 48px 0 12px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
  }
  .content .lede { font-size: 18px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 620px; }
  .content p { line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .content ul { line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 22px; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .content code {
    background: var(--bg-sunken);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 0 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  .content table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 14px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .content th, .content td {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 10px 12px;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .content th {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .muted-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .code {
    background: var(--code-bg);
    color: var(--code-fg);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre;
    margin: 8px 0 14px;
  }
  .code .prompt { color: var(--code-prompt); margin-right: 8px; }
  .code .k { color: var(--code-cmd); font-weight: 600; }
  .code .s { color: var(--code-str); }
  .code .hl { color: var(--accent); }
  .code .ok { color: var(--code-ok); display: inline-block; margin-top: 8px; }
  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 40px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .docs-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .sidebar { position: static; }
  }
</style>
